WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:18.811
"You found the spot where the treasure is buried?" Cole ran toward Maggie.

2
00:00:18.812 --> 00:00:21.554
Henry and the others rushed after him.

3
00:00:21.555 --> 00:00:24.915
Even Roger wandered over, looking curious.

4
00:00:24.916 --> 00:00:30.752
Maggie was still digging in the sand. Cole, Henry, Nathan, and Luke joined in.

5
00:00:30.753 --> 00:00:33.741
Soon they uncovered a large wooden trunk.

6
00:00:33.742 --> 00:00:37.470
"It looks like a real pirate chest!" Nathan said.

7
00:00:37.471 --> 00:00:40.387
He looked at Roger. "Doesn't it?"

8
00:00:40.388 --> 00:00:45.076
"Sure does." Roger winked. "Have fun with your treasure, kids.

9
00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:52.885
But watch out for Roger Redbeard!" He wandered off, whistling.

10
00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:56.317
"What are we waiting for, you guys?" Cole said eagerly.

11
00:00:56.318 --> 00:00:59.373
"Let's find out what our booty is!"

12
00:00:59.374 --> 00:01:04.606
Maggie opened the trunk. "Pirate hats!" she said.

13
00:01:04.607 --> 00:01:08.541
Luke grabbed one and then handed another one to Henry.

14
00:01:08.542 --> 00:01:12.033
"This one has your name on it, Henry."

15
00:01:12.034 --> 00:01:17.375
Cole pulled out more hats. "We each have one."

16
00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:22.098
Nathan grinned and put on his hat. "Do I look like a pirate?"

17
00:01:22.099 --> 00:01:27.612
Anna snorted. "You look like a kid with a dumb hat on to me," she said.

18
00:01:27.613 --> 00:01:30.490
Laughing, she tried her hat on too.

19
00:01:30.491 --> 00:01:35.388
Henry put on his hat and glanced at William. William hadn't touched his hat.

20
00:01:35.389 --> 00:01:41.284
And instead of laughing at how silly everyone looked, William had an angry scowl on his face.

21
00:01:41.285 --> 00:01:43.186
Henry moved closer to Cole.

22
00:01:43.187 --> 00:01:48.113
"Did you notice how strange William is acting today?" he whispered.

23
00:01:48.114 --> 00:01:52.097
"No." Cole glanced toward William. "What do you mean?"

24
00:01:52.098 --> 00:01:57.489
"He doesn't seem very excited about this treasure hunt," Henry whispered.

25
00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:01.297
"Do you think it's because he helped his parents hide the booty?

26
00:02:01.298 --> 00:02:04.373
Maybe he's trying not to give us any hints."

27
00:02:04.374 --> 00:02:11.518
"Maybe." Cole shrugged. "Or maybe he's bored because he does cool stuff like this all the time.

28
00:02:11.519 --> 00:02:15.193
His family is really rich, remember?" Cole went on.

29
00:02:15.194 --> 00:02:18.589
"They might have fancy treasure hunts every weekend."

30
00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:23.633
Meanwhile Luke had spotted a folded-up piece of paper inside the treasure chest.

31
00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:27.659
"I think this is our next clue," he said.

32
00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.917
Maggie unfolded the piece of paper.

33
00:02:29.918 --> 00:02:33.462
It was a drawing of a blue object along the beach.

34
00:02:33.463 --> 00:02:37.093
"What do you think this is supposed to be?" she murmured.

35
00:02:37.094 --> 00:02:39.695
"A swimming pool?" said Cole.

36
00:02:39.696 --> 00:02:43.305
"It looks like a little pond," said Henry.

37
00:02:43.306 --> 00:02:48.858
"Or a tide pool!" said Anna. "I bet that's what it is."

38
00:02:48.859 --> 00:02:59.143
Luke glanced around the beach. "Where's the closest one?" he asked.

39
00:02:59.144 --> 00:03:02.255
"Hmm . . . ," Anna said, thinking.

40
00:03:02.256 --> 00:03:04.854
"There are at least four tide pools near here.

41
00:03:04.855 --> 00:03:07.486
We should split up and check all of them."

42
00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:10.689
"Nathan and I will search together," Luke said.

43
00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:13.448
"I'll go with Henry," Maggie said.

44
00:03:13.449 --> 00:03:19.353
"Okay," Anna said. "I can search alone, since I know this beach better than anyone else."

45
00:03:19.354 --> 00:03:23.215
"I guess that leaves you and me," Cole told William with a grin.

46
00:03:23.216 --> 00:03:31.653
Anna told each pair where to go. Then the kids set out in different directions.

47
00:03:31.654 --> 00:03:37.137
It took Henry and Maggie about half an hour to find their tide pool and look for the treasure.

48
00:03:37.138 --> 00:03:40.033
But they didn't find anything.

49
00:03:40.034 --> 00:03:47.523
"Let's go see if the others found the treasure," Maggie said.

50
00:03:47.524 --> 00:03:52.029
They returned to the beach in front of the house. Cole was already there.

51
00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:55.078
"Did you find the booty?" Maggie asked him.

52
00:03:55.079 --> 00:03:58.304
"Nope," Cole said. "Did you?"

53
00:03:58.305 --> 00:04:02.421
Henry shook his head. "Where's William?" he asked.

54
00:04:02.422 --> 00:04:06.261
"William left right after we all split up," Cole replied.

55
00:04:06.262 --> 00:04:09.984
"He said he had to use the bathroom. But he never came back."

56
00:04:09.985 --> 00:04:15.440
Cole frowned, looking annoyed. "I had to find our tide pool all by myself."

57
00:04:15.441 --> 00:04:19.343
Before Henry could respond, he saw Anna walking toward them.

58
00:04:19.344 --> 00:04:23.454
"No luck, huh?" she asked. "Me neither."

59
00:04:23.455 --> 00:04:26.930
Just then they all heard a shout. It was Nathan.

60
00:04:26.931 --> 00:04:30.671
He was racing down the beach toward them, waving his arms.

61
00:04:30.672 --> 00:04:32.823
"We found it!" he cried.

62
00:04:32.824 --> 00:04:36.109
He skidded to a stop and then bent over to catch his breath.

63
00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:37.961
He started coughing.

64
00:04:37.962 --> 00:04:42.794
"Take it easy," Cole said. "Did you say you found the booty?"

65
00:04:42.795 --> 00:04:50.053
Nathan nodded. When he finally stopped coughing, he said, "Luke and I had some trouble finding our tide pool.

66
00:04:50.054 --> 00:04:54.535
But when we got there, we spotted something in the water right away.

67
00:04:54.536 --> 00:04:57.336
Come on, I'll show you."

68
00:04:57.337 --> 00:05:01.612
Henry, Maggie, Anna, and Cole followed him down the beach.

69
00:05:01.613 --> 00:05:05.149
When they reached Nathan's tide pool, Maggie gasped.

70
00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:08.651
"It's tear-shaped—like the picture on the map!"

71
00:05:08.652 --> 00:05:11.740
Luke was fishing a plastic container out of the water.

72
00:05:11.741 --> 00:05:14.485
William was there, watching him.

73
00:05:14.486 --> 00:05:20.699
"Is that the treasure?" Maggie wondered, eying the box. "It's pretty small."

74
00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:23.275
"Open it," Nathan urged.

75
00:05:23.276 --> 00:05:28.646
Luke opened the container. Then he frowned. "This can't be the treasure."

76
00:05:28.647 --> 00:05:35.802
"Why not?" Henry asked. "What's wrong?"

77
00:05:35.803 --> 00:05:39.183
Luke held the container out so they could all see inside.

78
00:05:39.184 --> 00:05:45.999
"There's nothing in here except a few soggy sticks of gum!"
